.TH ZFSDIFFSTREAM 1 "2026-11-24" "diffstream-tools 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
zfsdiffstream \- ZFS ZVOL and dataset file diff & apply utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zfsdiffstream
\-\-diff [--base snap] --change snap [--file relpath] [\-\-truncate size] [\-\-nocache] [\-v]
.br
.B zfsdiffstream
\-\-apply \-\-target file_or_dev [\-\-nocache] [\-\-noresize] [\-\-taildiscard]
.br
.B zfsdiffstream
[--base snap] --change snap [--file relpath] \-\-target file_or_dev [\-\-truncate size] [\-\-nocache] [\-\-noresize] [\-\-taildiscard] [\-v]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zfsdiffstream
computes block-level differences from ZFS send streams and emits or applies a wire-compatible
.B DIFFSTR1
stream (OP_TRUNCATE, OP_DATA, OP_HOLE, OP_EOF).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Emit a binary DIFFSTR1 delta stream to stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Read a DIFFSTR1 stream from stdin and apply to \fB\-\-target\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-base " src"
Baseline snapshot (if omitted, emits full sparse-aware stream including OP_HOLE packets for unmapped regions).
.TP
.BI \-\-change " src"
Modified snapshot to diff.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " relpath"
Relative path of a file within a ZFS filesystem dataset snapshot (resolves object ID via .zfs/snapshot inode).
.TP
.BI \-\-target " dst"
Destination file, LV, ZVOL, or block device.
.TP
.B \-\-nocache
Drop page cache pages via sync_file_range(2) and posix_fadvise(2).
.TP
.B \-\-noresize
Do not resize target on OP_TRUNCATE (required for fixed block devices). Fails if target < source.
.TP
.B \-\-taildiscard
With \fB\-\-noresize\fR, discard/zero trailing bytes past source EOF via BLKZEROOUT or FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print transfer statistics to stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-truncate " size"
Clamp source stream size to \fIsize\fR (supports K/M/G/T suffixes) for V2P migration onto smaller disks.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ZFS ZVOL to XFS sparse VM image migration:
zfsdiffstream --diff --base tank/vm@snap1 --change tank/vm@snap2 --nocache -v | zstd -T0 | ssh kvm-xfs "zstd -d | diffstream --apply --target /var/lib/libvirt/images/vm.raw --nocache"
.TP
.B Single file inside a ZFS dataset to remote Btrfs host:
zfsdiffstream --diff --base tank/vms@snap1 --change tank/vms@snap2 --file prod-db.raw --nocache -v | diffstream --apply --target /mnt/dr/prod-db.raw --nocache
.TP
.B ZFS ZVOL to fixed-size SAN LUN / partition:
zfsdiffstream --diff --base tank/vm@snap1 --change tank/vm@snap2 --nocache -v | diffstream --apply --target /dev/sdb1 --noresize --taildiscard --nocache
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffstream (1),
.BR thindiffstream (1),
.BR blkstream (1),
.BR zfs-send (8)
